rtant since  historically  she hulk is a comic book character known  for her meta humor  even going so far as to break the fourth  wall years before deadpool started doing  it in comics and films  it's over go home  maslany's small size in real life will  allow her to physically embody the  equally small  insecure side of walters but then as  someone who has played various clones in  orphan black she can easily use subtle  body language cues to show just how  different walter's personality becomes  when she transforms into she-hulk the  character of she-hulk isn't known for  having multiple personalities  but the duality of her nature is  something maslany is well suited for  at least as walters figures out her  powers and what they mean  she-hulk has gone through a lot of  different incarnations since her first  debut in the first issue of the savage  she-hulk in 1980.  the character that stanley and john  busama created back then was triggered  by rage  much like bruce banner but this  depiction didn't last long  far more popular was the version of  she-hulk written by john byrne wherein  walters saw her confidence bloom when  she became green  this depiction of the character was  self-aware comedic and has influenced  most other takes in the years since  it's entirely possible that the disney  plus series will pull influence from  those two eras  according to deadline sitcom director  cat cuero is involved in the show while  rick and morty's jessica gow is being  eyed to lead the writer's room all  of which implies a comedic focus unlike  the burn era though where in walters was  for all intents and purposes  permanently in she-hulk form it's  possible that maslany won't be green  all of the time or even most of the time  it's very likely that a big focus will  be paid to jennifer walters the lawyer  in which case the show may pull some  influence from the comic book run by  writer attorney charles sol  who put a lot of emphasis on that  element and specifically 